The [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]] is peopled by shades: shadows in the shape of men and women, walking its streets, standing in its queues and sitting in its seats. They say nothing. Nothing can be felt in that place, living or dead, and none of them has ever been touched. Looked at straight on they thin to almost nothing, and they are clearest at the edge of vision.

The Party found them more solid the longer they stayed. By the time they had opened the buildings around the [[Geography/Black and White/Plaza|plaza]], the shades had grown opaque, and now and then one would stand still, seem to face the Party for a moment, and fade back into the crowd.

Some carry a caught sound inside them. A few in the [[Geography/Black and White/Soundscape Theaters|Soundscape Theaters]] sparkled and chimed with faint piano music, with moth wing scales floating inside them. Held a [[Phenomena/Voice Box|voice box]] to one and the scales pull free, and the shades turn hostile. One threw its own head as a missile and grew a new one. They have no bones; killed, they lose their shape and leave their moth scales floating where they stood.
